queries dilute ranking and return shallow results for each topic.\n\n### Step 4: Use the Documentation\n\nIncorporate the fetched documentation into your response:\n\n- Answer the user's question using current, accurate information\n- Include relevant code examples from the docs\n- Cite the library version when relevant\n\n## Guidelines\n\n- **Be specific**: Describe what to look up in the library's documentation, but keep each query to a single concept\n- **One topic per query**: Split multi-topic questions into separate `query-docs` calls — resolve the library ID once, then query per concept, unless the question is about how the concepts interact\n- **Version awareness**: When users mention versions (\"Next.js 15\", \"React 19\"), use version-specific library IDs if available from the resolution step\n- **Prefer official sources**: When multiple matches exist, prefer official/primary packages over community forks\n"},"type":"raw"},"obs_mudlycth_cdb01802d05d":{"observation":{"hookType":"post_tool_use","id":"obs_mudlycth_cdb01802d05d","origin":{"capturedAt":"2026-09-23T04:33:35.298Z","channel":"tool","detail":"Bash"},"raw":{"tool_input":{"command":"sed -n '590,605p' /home/chris/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"},"tool_name":"Bash","tool_output":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1022)\nTotal output lines: 16\n\n- The Task 8 coordinator rollout did not complete a full precommit, production build, or browser pass. Focused tests and subagent reports are not full integration verification; rerun those gates before treating branch-consolidation changes as complete. Keep geometry conversion helpers scoped inside their traversal function: an out-of-scope helper in `studioOutline.ts` caused the initial typecheck failure. [Task 8]\n- For resize behavior, add regressions for popup absence and first-column 1u-to-1.5u overlap before editing. Edge-alignment expectations must reflect inward-edge `Auto (make room)` semantics; normalize both bare IDs and `objects.<id>` constraint refs so blocked movement is detected. [Task 8][Task 9]\n- Running pnpm scripts from a `/tmp` checkout with symlinked `node_modules` can raise `ERR_PNPM_UNSAFE_MODULES_DIR`; prefer the real/original checkout, or use the recorded `pnpm_config_verify_deps_before_run` workaround only for verification. [Task 9]\n- Do not infer GitHub promotion, deployment, production changes, or branch retirement from a local candidate, a prepared PR, or local push output. Promotion was paused; verify remote refs independently when authority resumes. [Task 10]\n- Do not blame a second matrix or missing bridge for outline failure before tracing region closing: the reproduced first failure was `Gap closing failed to preserve closed occupied geometry`; exact-radius offset contraction can lose topology. Preserve explicit holes while filling incidental voids through policy, and run focused engine regressions plus GUI precommit/build/browser outline checks before calling a change complete. [Task 11]\n- Do not pre-validate a drag in a worker before committing it; `StudioCanvas` waits for `useLayoutAnalysis(candidate)` and `BoardStudio.move()` refuses edits while stale/pending, causing blocking/snapback. Commit immediately, defer `addOutline()` until the current `LayoutReport`, and invalidate obsolete worker output on edits, undo, imports, and proj…22 tokens truncated…]\n- A clean comparison checkout reproduced 287 engine passes plus 18 DXF fixture failures. Report those fixtures as pre-existing, never as a green engine suite. Initial snapping-menu checks were asynchronous; use `expect.poll` for bounding-box assertions. [Task 12]\n- If precommit reports Markdownlint MD041, restore `# Changelog` as the first top-level heading before rerunning. [Task 12]\n- Before row/column assertions, convert a `free` arrangement to columns/rows; a scalar thumb pitch yields `must be array`. Do not use `resizeCluster(..., mode: 'fill')` for BHK: it fills intentional holes. [Task 13]\n- The BHK migrated PCB is not byte-identical: normalized footprint/copper/net content matched, but parametric trigonometry changed outline coordinates by up to ~0.000671 mm. Attribute unscoped precommit/prebuild vendor/library failures only after isolating vendor state. [Task 13]\n- `PCB preview unavailable: Unable to create WebGL2 context` in Xvfb is an environment rendering limit; rerun Chromium with SwiftShader for KiCanvas/browser CAD checks. [Task 13]\n- `plate_gap / 2` entered through the stack editor can self-reference and throw `Cyclic parameter: plate_gap`; reject/rewrite self-referential parameter expressions before storing. Material fit for an unlinked case must use local dimensions, topology changes must update overridden assemblies without discarding other customizations, and name-only Setup drafts must not restore stale pitch. A column-guide alignment failure (`Solved layout does not satisfy this driving rule`) needs solver-consistent guide geometry. Passing focused engine tests alone did not expose these five regressions; retain targeted Vitest, Playwright, and direct-engine probes. [Task 14]\n\n# Task Group: BHK example restoration, enclosure completion boundary, and opacity diagnosis\n\nscope: restore and validate the BHK GUI example without claiming a fabrication-ready enclosure; route ambiguous opacity reports to a concrete preview-versus-wizard reproduction\n"},"sessionId":"01a0cc85-d15f-7fc2-a114-2710e0599e22","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:33:35.298Z","toolInput":{"command":"sed -n '590,605p' /home/chris/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"},"toolName":"Bash","toolOutput":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1022)\nTotal output lines: 16\n\n- The Task 8 coordinator rollout did not complete a full precommit, production build, or browser pass. Focused tests and subagent reports are not full integration verification; rerun those gates before treating branch-consolidation changes as complete. Keep geometry conversion helpers scoped inside their traversal function: an out-