user said “push to cloud and contiune in cloud” -> transfer the exact verified state from a branch, retain local edits, and do not reset or merge locally. [Task 3]\n- when the user expected bundled libraries such as BHK to be visible instead of an empty list -> clearly distinguish the built-in catalogue from user-created injections, and make customization create an editable override without mutating bundled sources. [Task 4]\n- when the user asked to “add the 3d models to existing footprints and import generic kicad footprints to convert them to ergogen” -> connect footprint geometry, model placement, clearance, and case generation in one understandable workflow. [Task 5]\n- when the user asked to “make a cleaner break from legacy ergogen” and chose “Native only” plus “Foundation + focused GUI” -> treat the native object/configuration model as the runtime contract; do not expand legacy compatibility or assume broad migration is required. [Task 7]\n- when the user asked for work in the enclosure checkout and “a living architecture overview” -> keep `DEVELOPMENT.md` synchronized with implementation; retain direct visual QA and state its boundary from fabrication readiness. [Task 7]\n- when the user required “Commit edits immediately,” editing while analysis is pending, and no snapback from delayed workers -> persist source changes cumulatively without validation-before-commit; one coordinator must own revisions, draft geometry, workers, and publication. [Task 8]\n- when the user said “we want it to be fast, not interrupt the user” and chose “Keep move and flag” -> commit a move on release, keep it visible when asynchronous validation finds a conflict, and block fabrication/export rather than reverting it. [Task 11]\n- when the user requested “outline should be automatic with an option to disable auto outline only” -> use one persisted automatic-outline setting, default enabled; when disabled, retain the current outline and manual rebuild. [Task 11]\n- when the user said the selection popup “likes to cover up the keyboard” and chose “One combined pill (Recommended)” -> do not auto-open `SelectionPopover`; use one manually opened Inspector with collapsible `Objects`, `Selection`, and `Design` sections. [Task 8][Task 9]\n- when the user chose “Make room automatically (Recommended)” -> resize through one atomic shared path that compensates surrounding spacing, preserves authored offsets/expressions, and does not accumulate generated adjustments. [Task 8][Task 9]\n- when selecting a branch model, the user chose “Studio as main line,” “main in both,” and “Archive tags” -> make Studio the intended canonical direction, archive exact tips before deletion, and preserve dirty originals in isolated worktrees. [Task 10]\n- when the user said “lets jjust test locally for now” -> immediately stop promotion, deployment, branch retirement, and all further remote mutations, even if earlier promotion approval existed. [Task 10]\n- when choosing outline semantics, the user selected “fill incidental gaps” while preserving explicit cutouts -> automatic outlines should fill incidental voids without silently removing intentional cutouts/protected gaps. [Task 11]\n- when the user reported “missing previews, some display issues,” or an outline was not drawing despite being technically valid -> require direct browser rendering checks, not only generator/unit success. [Task 2][Task 5]\n- preserve existing KiCad/BHK changes when extending the workflow; do not revert unrelated engine or enclosure work. [Task 1][Task 5]\n- when changing setup/layout, preserve authored units, formulas, overrides, footprint ownership, constraints, project/camera state, and unrelated worktree edits -> do not regenerate layouts or destructively migrate setup state. [Task 12]\n- for setup UI, use staged edits with one undoable “Apply”, explicit invalid-expression feedback without source mutation, compact primary controls, and expandable secondary controls. [Task 12]\n- when the user asks for “proper col and row support” -> preserve semantic `cell: [column, row]` matrix structure and editable axes instead of flattening placements to absolute coordinates. [Task 13]\n- when asked to “review all recent changes” -> inspect recent commits and current uncommitted edits across the active nested CAD checkout; preserve useful capabilities and do not reset it for a narrow review. [Task 14]\n\n## Reusable knowledge\n\n"},"sessionId":"01a0cc85-d15f-7fc2-a114-2710e0599e22","timestamp":"2026-09-23T04:34:29.741Z","toolInput":{"command":"sed -n '530,555p' /home/chris/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md"},"toolName":"Bash","toolOutput":"\n- when offered checkout scopes, the user chose “Latest CAD workflow” -> focus on `enclosure-work/ergogen-gui` and preserve existing work rather than comparing or resetting all versions. [Task 1]\n- when asked how far to simplify, the user chose “Merge overlapping workflows” and requested reducing “redundant features and needless complexity” -> consolidate duplicate controls/state with regression coverage; do not broadly remove useful capabilities. [Task 1]\n- when the user wanted the battery connector close to a switch without PCB footprint overlap “in terms of what happens on the PCB” -> separate editable component placement from MX key-spacing constraints while retaining PCB collision analysis. [Task 2]\n- when the user said “push to cloud and contiune in cloud” -> transfer the exact verified state from a branch, retain local edits, and do not reset or merge locally. [Task 3]\n- when the user expected bundled libraries such as BHK to be visible instead of an empty list -> clearly distinguish the built-in catalogue from user-created injections, and make customization create an editable override without mutating bundled sources. [Task 4]\n- when the user asked to “add the 3d models to existing footprints and import generic kicad footprints to convert them to ergogen” -> connect footprint geometry, model placement, clearance, and case 